# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Takrifkan Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function takes the model as a dictionary with three keys. Each one accepts either a single float, which applies uniformly along the chain, or a list that specifies the value site by site. Lists have $L-1$ entries for `hopping_amplitude`, because an open chain has one fewer bond than sites, and $L$ entries for `on_site_interaction` and `chemical_potential`.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi ini menerima model sebagai kamus dengan tiga kunci. Setiap satu menerima sama ada satu float tunggal, yang digunakan secara seragam sepanjang rantai, atau senarai yang menentukan nilai tapak demi tapak. Senarai mempunyai $L-1$ entri untuk `hopping_amplitude`, kerana rantai terbuka mempunyai satu ikatan kurang daripada bilangan tapak, dan $L$ entri untuk `on_site_interaction` dan `chemical_potential`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses a uniform chain of 31 sites with a repulsive interaction $U/t_h = 8$. A uniform chemical potential contributes only a global phase when the particle number is fixed, so this example sets it to zero. The chemical potential matters only when it varies from site to site, for example, to add disorder or a single impurity.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan rantai seragam dengan 31 tapak dan interaksi tolakan $U/t_h = 8$. Keupayaan kimia seragam hanya menyumbang fasa global apabila bilangan zarah tetap, jadi contoh ini menetapkannya kepada sifar. Keupayaan kimia hanya penting apabila ia berbeza dari tapak ke tapak, contohnya, untuk menambah gangguan atau satu kekotoran tunggal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the Trotter schedule {#set-the-trotter-schedule}"
msgstr "Tetapkan jadual Trotter {#set-the-trotter-schedule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `simulation` dictionary holds the time step ($\\Delta t$) and the number of Trotter steps, and the total evolution time is their product. Larger steps reach later times at fixed circuit depth but incur more Trotter error, which grows with $U$ because the Hamiltonian terms commute less. The published hardware study used $\\Delta t = 0.15$ for $U/t_h = 8$ [\\[2\\]](#references), and this tutorial uses the same value. Circuit depth grows linearly in the step count and does not depend on $L$ at all.\n"
msgstr "Kamus `simulation` memegang langkah masa ($\\Delta t$) dan bilangan langkah Trotter, dan jumlah masa evolusi ialah hasil darab keduanya. Langkah yang lebih besar mencapai masa yang lebih lewat pada kedalaman litar tetap tetapi menimbulkan lebih banyak ralat Trotter, yang bertambah dengan $U$ kerana sebutan Hamiltonian kurang berkomut. Kajian perkakasan yang diterbitkan menggunakan $\\Delta t = 0.15$ untuk $U/t_h = 8$ [\\[2\\]](#references), dan tutorial ini menggunakan nilai yang sama. Kedalaman litar bertambah secara linear dengan bilangan langkah dan langsung tidak bergantung pada $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the initial state {#prepare-the-initial-state}"
msgstr "Sediakan keadaan awal {#prepare-the-initial-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each site holds two spin orbitals, so an $L$-site chain uses $2L$ qubits. The initial state is a Fock occupation string with one character per site:\n"
msgstr "Setiap tapak memegang dua orbital spin, jadi rantai $L$ tapak menggunakan $2L$ qubit. Keadaan awal ialah rentetan penghunian Fock dengan satu aksara bagi setiap tapak:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\texttt{empty (e)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{up (u)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{down (d)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,1), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{both (b)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,1).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\texttt{empty (e)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{up (u)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{down (d)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,1), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{both (b)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,1).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The string is read least significant site first, so the rightmost character is site 0 and the physical site index of character $k$ counted from the left is $i = L - 1 - k$. The string `udud` therefore means site 0 is `d`, site 1 is `u`, site 2 is `d`, and site 3 is `u`.\n"
msgstr "Rentetan dibaca bermula dengan tapak paling tidak signifikan, jadi aksara paling kanan ialah tapak 0 dan indeks tapak fizikal bagi aksara $k$ yang dikira dari kiri ialah $i = L - 1 - k$. Oleh itu rentetan `udud` bermaksud tapak 0 ialah `d`, tapak 1 ialah `u`, tapak 2 ialah `d`, dan tapak 3 ialah `u`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, prepare a half-filled Néel state, alternating `u` and `d`, with the central site replaced by a vacancy. The vacancy is the disturbance whose spreading is tracked.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, sediakan keadaan Néel separuh penuh, berselang-seli `u` dan `d`, dengan tapak tengah digantikan dengan kekosongan. Kekosongan ialah gangguan yang penyebarannya dijejaki.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the observables {#build-the-observables}"
msgstr "Bina observable {#build-the-observables}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each observable is a dictionary that represents a weighted sum of products of occupation operators:\n"
msgstr "Setiap observable ialah kamus yang mewakili hasil tambah berpemberat bagi hasil darab operator penghunian:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{\\alpha} c_{\\alpha} \\prod_{(\\sigma, j) \\in T_{\\alpha}} n_{j,\\sigma}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{\\alpha} c_{\\alpha} \\prod_{(\\sigma, j) \\in T_{\\alpha}} n_{j,\\sigma}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every entry of `operators` is one term $T_{\\alpha}$, written as a list of `[name, site]` pairs that multiply together, and the matching entry of `coefficients` is its weight. The two names are `\"Nup\"` for $n_{j,\\uparrow}$ and `\"Ndn\"` for $n_{j,\\downarrow}$. A single one-point observable $n_{3,\\uparrow}$ is written as follows:\n"
msgstr "Setiap entri `operators` ialah satu sebutan $T_{\\alpha}$, ditulis sebagai senarai pasangan `[name, site]` yang didarabkan bersama, dan entri `coefficients` yang sepadan ialah pemberatnya. Kedua-dua nama ialah `\"Nup\"` untuk $n_{j,\\uparrow}$ dan `\"Ndn\"` untuk $n_{j,\\downarrow}$. Satu observable satu titik tunggal $n_{3,\\uparrow}$ ditulis seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next cell prints the smallest complete set of inputs the function accepts, which is useful as a shape reference while reading the code that follows.\n"
msgstr "Sel seterusnya mencetak set input lengkap terkecil yang diterima oleh fungsi, yang berguna sebagai rujukan bentuk semasa membaca kod yang berikut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three groups of observables are needed. The charge density $n_i = n_{i\\uparrow} + n_{i\\downarrow}$ and the local spin $S^z_i = (n_{i\\uparrow} - n_{i\\downarrow})/2$ are both two-term sums over the same operators, differing only in their coefficients. The spin correlator $S^z_i S^z_{i_*}$ between site $i$ and the vacancy site expands into four two-point terms with coefficients $\\pm 1/4$.\n"
msgstr "Tiga kumpulan observable diperlukan. Ketumpatan cas $n_i = n_{i\\uparrow} + n_{i\\downarrow}$ dan spin setempat $S^z_i = (n_{i\\uparrow} - n_{i\\downarrow})/2$ kedua-duanya ialah hasil tambah dua sebutan ke atas operator yang sama, hanya berbeza pada pekalinya. Korelator spin $S^z_i S^z_{i_*}$ antara tapak $i$ dan tapak kekosongan berkembang kepada empat sebutan dua titik dengan pekali $\\pm 1/4$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Occupation operators commute, so the order of factors within a term is irrelevant, but the order of the `observables` list fixes the order of the returned values. The code records an index for each group while it builds the list. The correlator skips the vacancy site, where the product would repeat a factor.\n"
msgstr "Operator penghunian berkomut, jadi susunan faktor dalam sesuatu sebutan tidak relevan, tetapi susunan senarai `observables` menetapkan susunan nilai yang dikembalikan. Kod merekodkan indeks bagi setiap kumpulan semasa ia membina senarai. Korelator melangkau tapak kekosongan, di mana hasil darab akan mengulangi satu faktor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan pada perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial has no transpilation step. The function performs the following steps internally [\\[2\\]](#references), and you cannot configure them from the notebook:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini tidak mempunyai langkah transpilasi. Fungsi ini melakukan langkah berikut secara dalaman [\\[2\\]](#references), dan anda tidak boleh mengkonfigurasinya daripada notebook:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maps the fermionic modes to qubits under an ordering chosen to keep Pauli weights low on a heavy-hex lattice\n"
msgstr "Memetakan mod fermion kepada qubit di bawah susunan yang dipilih untuk mengekalkan pemberat Pauli rendah pada kekisi heavy-hex\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Uses a fermionic SWAP network so every hopping term becomes a two-qubit rotation\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan rangkaian SWAP fermion supaya setiap sebutan lompatan menjadi putaran dua qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embeds the chain along a path that avoids weak qubits\n"
msgstr "Membenamkan rantai di sepanjang laluan yang mengelakkan qubit lemah\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applies dynamical decoupling and Pauli twirling during compilation\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan dynamical decoupling dan Pauli twirling semasa kompilasi\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You choose the backend and the shot count. The function takes a backend name as a string, so this tutorial selects the least busy device large enough for the chain and passes its name.\n"
msgstr "Anda memilih backend dan bilangan shot. Fungsi ini menerima nama backend sebagai rentetan, jadi tutorial ini memilih peranti paling kurang sibuk yang cukup besar untuk rantai dan menghantar namanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The smallest signal that you need to resolve sets the shot count. The charge tracer reaches amplitudes near $0.15$, but the connected spin tracer peaks around $0.04$, roughly four times smaller. The published study used 20,000 shots per circuit for this reason [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Isyarat terkecil yang perlu anda leraikan menentukan bilangan shot. Pengesan cas mencapai amplitud sekitar $0.15$, tetapi pengesan spin bersambung memuncak sekitar $0.04$, kira-kira empat kali lebih kecil. Kajian yang diterbitkan menggunakan 20,000 shot bagi setiap litar atas sebab ini [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute by using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-by-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan dengan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-by-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, submit the simulation. `run` returns a job handle immediately rather than blocking.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, hantar simulasi. `run` mengembalikan pemegang job serta-merta dan bukannya menyekat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `job.status()` to follow progress and `job.result()` to block until the job finishes. The result is a mapping whose `observable_expectation_values` entry is indexed first by observable, in the order they were supplied, and then by time. There are `step_count + 1` time points because the value at $t=0$ is included.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan `job.status()` untuk mengikuti kemajuan dan `job.result()` untuk menyekat sehingga job selesai. Hasilnya ialah pemetaan yang entri `observable_expectation_values`nya diindeks dahulu mengikut observable, mengikut susunan ia dibekalkan, dan kemudian mengikut masa. Terdapat `step_count + 1` titik masa kerana nilai pada $t=0$ disertakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan pulangkan hasil dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconstruct the correlators {#reconstruct-the-correlators}"
msgstr "Bina semula korelator {#reconstruct-the-correlators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split the flat array back into the three groups using the indices recorded earlier, then form the two tracer correlators. The charge tracer is the change in per-site density relative to $t=0$:\n"
msgstr "Pisahkan tatasusunan rata kembali kepada tiga kumpulan menggunakan indeks yang direkodkan sebelum ini, kemudian bentuk dua korelator pengesan. Pengesan cas ialah perubahan ketumpatan bagi setiap tapak relatif kepada $t=0$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C^c_i(t) = \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(t) + n_{i\\downarrow}(t) \\rangle - \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(0) + n_{i\\downarrow}(0) \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C^c_i(t) = \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(t) + n_{i\\downarrow}(t) \\rangle - \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(0) + n_{i\\downarrow}(0) \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The spin tracer is the connected correlator between each site and the vacancy site $i_*$:\n"
msgstr "Pengesan spin ialah korelator bersambung antara setiap tapak dan tapak kekosongan $i_*$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C^s_i(t) = 4 \\left( \\langle S^z_i S^z_{i_*} \\rangle - \\langle S^z_i \\rangle \\langle S^z_{i_*} \\rangle \\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C^s_i(t) = 4 \\left( \\langle S^z_i S^z_{i_*} \\rangle - \\langle S^z_i \\rangle \\langle S^z_{i_*} \\rangle \\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are built from Fock-basis operators, so they come from the same measured bitstrings and the second one costs no extra hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-duanya dibina daripada operator asas Fock, jadi ia datang daripada rentetan bit terukur yang sama dan yang kedua tidak memerlukan pelaksanaan perkakasan tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you constructed the observables, the code recorded the position of each charge (`charge_indices`), spin (`spin_indices`), and spin-correlation (`correlator_indices`) operator in the list. Because the simulator returns the expectation values in the same order, you can use these positions to extract the corresponding results. For the spin correlations, the code also uses `correlator_sites` to place each result at the correct lattice position, and leaves the vacancy as `NaN`.\n"
msgstr "Apabila anda membina observable, kod merekodkan kedudukan setiap operator cas (`charge_indices`), spin (`spin_indices`), dan korelasi spin (`correlator_indices`) dalam senarai. Oleh sebab simulator mengembalikan nilai jangkaan dalam susunan yang sama, anda boleh menggunakan kedudukan ini untuk mengekstrak hasil yang sepadan. Bagi korelasi spin, kod juga menggunakan `correlator_sites` untuk meletakkan setiap hasil pada kedudukan kekisi yang betul, dan membiarkan kekosongan sebagai `NaN`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the wavefronts {#visualize-the-wavefronts}"
msgstr "Visualkan muka gelombang {#visualize-the-wavefronts}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you plot each correlator as a heatmap of space and time, the light cone is directly visible. Time flows downward, and the horizontal axis is the position along the chain.\n"
msgstr "Jika anda memplot setiap korelator sebagai peta haba ruang dan masa, kon cahaya dapat dilihat secara langsung. Masa mengalir ke bawah, dan paksi mengufuk ialah kedudukan di sepanjang rantai.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c75549b7-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c75549b7-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extract the wavefront velocities {#extract-the-wavefront-velocities}"
msgstr "Ekstrak halaju muka gelombang {#extract-the-wavefront-velocities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Turn the heatmaps into numbers by following the detection protocol from the published study [\\[2\\]](#references). At each time slice, symmetrize the spatial profile about the vacancy, which averages away the antisymmetric part of the hardware noise, normalize by the largest off-center amplitude, and record the outermost site above a threshold. Detections are then cut into runs of consecutive time steps, and only the longest run is fit, which keeps the early-time transient out of the result.\n"
msgstr "Tukarkan peta haba kepada nombor dengan mengikuti protokol pengesanan daripada kajian yang diterbitkan [\\[2\\]](#references). Pada setiap hirisan masa, simetrikan profil ruang tentang kekosongan, yang memurnikan bahagian antisimetri hingar perkakasan, normalkan dengan amplitud luar pusat terbesar, dan rekodkan tapak paling luar yang melebihi ambang. Pengesanan kemudian dipotong kepada larian langkah masa berturutan, dan hanya larian terpanjang dipadankan, yang mengekalkan peralihan awal daripada hasil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fitted velocity depends on the detection threshold and the trimming quantile, and that sensitivity dominates the shot noise. Scan both and report the median with the full envelope, as the published analysis does.\n"
msgstr "Halaju yang dipadankan bergantung pada ambang pengesanan dan kuantil pemangkasan, dan kepekaan itu mengatasi hingar shot. Imbas kedua-duanya dan laporkan median dengan sampul penuh, seperti yang dilakukan oleh analisis yang diterbitkan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/640db359-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/640db359-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Drawing the detections back onto the heatmaps shows whether the algorithm tracked\n"
"the leading edge. Filled markers are the detections that entered\n"
"the fit. Open markers were cut by the masking rules, either because they sit too\n"
"close to the vacancy, too close to the chain end, or were late enough that the front has\n"
"broadened and its position is no longer sharp. The dashed line is the fit over the\n"
"times it used, and its slope is the velocity in each panel title.\n"
msgstr "Melukis semula pengesanan ke atas peta haba menunjukkan sama ada algoritma itu menjejaki pinggir hadapan. Penanda berisi ialah pengesanan yang digunakan dalam penyuaian. Penanda terbuka dipotong oleh peraturan penyembunyian, sama ada kerana terlalu dekat dengan kekosongan, terlalu dekat dengan hujung rantai, atau terlalu lewat sehingga bahagian hadapan telah melebar dan kedudukannya tidak lagi tajam. Garis putus-putus ialah penyuaian ke atas masa yang digunakan, dan kecerunannya ialah halaju dalam setiap tajuk panel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The vacancy column is marked below the axis. The charge clips there because its value\n"
"is of order one, and spin has no value there, so it is drawn in gray.\n"
msgstr "Lajur kekosongan ditandakan di bawah paksi. Cas terpangkas di situ kerana nilainya berada pada susunan satu, dan spin tidak mempunyai nilai di situ, jadi ia dilukis dalam warna kelabu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The charge cone opens wider than the spin cone. Both disturbances leave the same\n"
"defect at the same moment and travel outward at different speeds.\n"
msgstr "Kon cas terbuka lebih luas daripada kon spin. Kedua-dua gangguan meninggalkan kecacatan yang sama pada saat yang sama dan bergerak ke luar pada kelajuan yang berbeza.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/25192e92-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/25192e92-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The charge front outruns the spin front. A hole in a one-dimensional Mott background does not travel as an electron. Instead, it fractionalizes into a holon carrying the charge and a spinon carrying the spin disturbance, and at $U/t_h = 8$ the spinon is the slower of the two.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian hadapan cas memintas bahagian hadapan spin. Lubang dalam latar Mott satu dimensi tidak bergerak sebagai elektron. Sebaliknya, ia berpecah kepada holon yang membawa cas dan spinon yang membawa gangguan spin, dan pada $U/t_h = 8$ spinon ialah yang lebih perlahan antara keduanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ordering depends on the interaction. At $U = 0$, the model is free fermions with $v_c = 2$ and $v_s = 4$, so spin is faster. Repulsion suppresses spin transport while leaving charge transport nearly untouched, and by $U/t_h = 8$ the published hardware values are $v_c = 1.78$ and $v_s = 1.46$ [\\[2\\]](#references). Rerunning with several values of $U$ and plotting $v_s / v_c$ maps the crossover.\n"
msgstr "Susunan itu bergantung pada interaksi. Pada $U = 0$, model ialah fermion bebas dengan $v_c = 2$ dan $v_s = 4$, jadi spin lebih laju. Tolakan menyekat pengangkutan spin sambil hampir tidak menjejaskan pengangkutan cas, dan pada $U/t_h = 8$ nilai perkakasan yang diterbitkan ialah $v_c = 1.78$ dan $v_s = 1.46$ [\\[2\\]](#references). Menjalankan semula dengan beberapa nilai $U$ dan memplot $v_s / v_c$ memetakan peralihan tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note these caveats on the numbers. Threshold-based detection is biased slightly low, so a charge velocity a few percent under the published value is expected. The spin envelope is wide because the connected correlator sits closer to the noise floor, which is why the median of the scan rather than a single fit is quoted.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan beberapa kaveat pada nombor ini. Pengesanan berasaskan ambang berat sebelah sedikit ke bawah, jadi halaju cas yang beberapa peratus di bawah nilai yang diterbitkan adalah dijangka. Sampul spin adalah lebar kerana korelator bersambung lebih hampir dengan aras hingar, itulah sebabnya median imbasan dipetik dan bukannya satu penyuaian tunggal.\n"

